credd-2 -> credd.badrecord  file:temp/atf_comp/credd.Import/home/.ssh/gli.ssim  remoteurl:ssh://git@nowhere.example.com/x/y.git  comment:"serverurl carries no scheme://host, so the token has no credential name; skipped"
credd-2 -> The tokens stay in the records, so a gli built without credd, in another checkout on this machine, keeps working.
credd-2 -> Once every gli on this machine is built with credd, run gli -auth in each checkout and answer - at its token prompt to drop the token from the record.
credd-2 -> credd.rewrite  file:temp/atf_comp/credd.Import/home/.ssh/gli.ssim  n_record:1
credd-2 -> credd.badfile  file:temp/atf_comp/credd.Import/home/.ssh/bin.token  comment:"not a text file holding a token; skipped"
credd-2 -> temp/atf_comp/credd.Import/home/.ssh/me.token holds a token, 63 bytes, looks like aws.
credd-2 ->   It becomes credential me, the file's content as the secret.
credd-2 ->   Retrieve it with credd -show:me, or eval "$(credd -show:me)" for a shell fragment.
credd-2 ->   The file stays until you remove it.
credd-2 -> credd.add  cred:me  kind:aws  linkto:""  perm:""
credd-2 -> temp/atf_comp/credd.Import/home/.ssh/id_locked is a private key, behind a passphrase.
credd-2 ->   It becomes credential id_locked, kind sshkey, sealed under the master password.
credd-2 ->   The daemon loads it into the agent at temp/atf_comp/credd.Import/home/.ssh/ssh_auth_sock; with SSH_AUTH_SOCK naming that, ssh finds it.
credd-2 ->   Once the key is in the store the file is no longer needed, and you can remove it.  credd never removes it.
credd-2 -> credd.badkey  name:id_locked  comment:"wrong passphrase, or ssh-keygen cannot read it; skipped"
credd-2 -> temp/atf_comp/credd.Import/home/.ssh/id_plain is a private key.
credd-2 ->   It becomes credential id_plain, kind sshkey, sealed under the master password.
credd-2 ->   The daemon loads it into the agent at temp/atf_comp/credd.Import/home/.ssh/ssh_auth_sock; with SSH_AUTH_SOCK naming that, ssh finds it.
credd-2 ->   Once the key is in the store the file is no longer needed, and you can remove it.  credd never removes it.
credd-2 -> credd.add  cred:id_plain  kind:sshkey  linkto:""  perm:""
credd-2 -> credd.import  n_add:3  n_cred:3  comment:"credd -list shows the store; credd -start serves it"
